Problem Statement

When I lose track of time due to video games and doomscrolling social media, I have to make sure I either get to school on time or sleep at a normal time which is frustrating because video games and social media can get super addicting and I lose track of time. I think this happens because social media and video games is intended to make you lose track of your time. What I wish happened instead is that social media shuts down for the night to prevent everyone from doomscrolling until the next day.

Self-Check

- Would a stranger understand this without me explaining it?
A stranger would definitely understand this, people lose track of time all the time due to video games and social media.

- Does it name a specific person, not a demographic?
It names people who play video games from dusk until dawn, or people who doomscroll social media constantly.

- Does it avoid naming a solution?
